	"id": "iron-curtain",
	"name": "Operation Iron Curtain — Layered IADS",
	"description": "A full integrated air-defence system spread in DEPTH across the northern theatre — ~75 hostile units from 60 km out to 160 km deep, across a 120-degree arc. You CANNOT just fly in and bomb a target: an airborne AWACS + three early-warning radars cue a dispersed belt of seven NASAMS batteries (25 km reach) and ~30 fighters (Su-35 Flankers, enemy F-35s, Rafales) flying CAP, with five command compounds each ringed by SA-15 Tor SHORAD and ZSU-23 point-defence guns, plus localized Krasukha jammers and a laser CIWS at the main HQ. Peel it back in phases — and you'll want to SWITCH AIRFRAMES: (1) AIR SUPERIORITY — a stealth BVR jet (F-22 / F-35 / F-47) to kill the enemy AWACS and thin the CAP; (2) SEAD/DEAD — an F-16 or F-15 with AGM-88 HARMs to blind the EWR net and roll back the NASAMS belt; (3) STRIKE — once the SAMs are down, a B-2 (200+ SDBs), the SR-72 (hypersonic SDB toss from standoff), or a strike fighter with SDBs to flatten the command compounds from outside the surviving SHORAD rings. Friendly E-767 + RQ-4 give you the picture — keep the drone alive. SPAWN AT THE SOUTHERN EDGE: the whole IADS is laid out to your NORTH.",
	"autoSpawn": false,
	"triangleSideM": 240000,

